# winemac: raw mouse read with GCMouse
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11799 state=opened
# This merge request improves the competitive gaming experience in games such as Overwatch and Marvel Rivals on macOS. ~~It contains two functional changes~~

<s>winemac: replace hidden cursor with transparent cursor</s> (moved to separate MR [!11880](/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11880))

~~On macOS 26, moving the mouse while the native cursor is hidden can cause frame presentation to synchronize with the display refresh rate, even when VSync is disabled. In Overwatch, for example, the frame rate can drop from 250–300 FPS to 120 FPS, the refresh rate of the built-in display, whenever the mouse moves.~~

~~Using a transparent cursor instead of calling `[NSCursor hide]` avoids this hidden-cursor synchronization path while keeping the cursor visually hidden.~~

~~A demonstration of the problem is available in this~~

~~https://www.reddit.com/r/macgaming/comments/1umok4l/the_game_runs_a_stable_250300fps_but_as_soon_as_i/~~

winemac.drv: Add GCMouse raw input support.

The existing macOS input path derives mouse movement from `NSEvent` events routed through WindowServer. This is not equivalent to Windows raw input: movement delivery may be coalesced or synchronized with display updates, and the deltas may be affected by macOS pointer acceleration and sensitivity settings.

The new path activates `GCMouse` when an application registers a Windows raw-input mouse device. In testing, `GCMouse`delivers unaccelerated movement deltas at the mouse’s full 1000 Hz polling rate. It also decouples mouse movement from the regular `NSEvent` stream, preventing movement delivery from depending on unrelated keyboard, button, or scroll events.

Setting `WINE_DISABLE_GCMOUSE=1` disables GCMouse and falls back to `NSEvent` based mouse input for compatibility with older games.

**Testing**

I tested these changes by playing Marvel Rivals, Overwatch, and Kingdom Come: Deliverance II (KCD2).

